  "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. The fix is complete.\n\n**The issue:** The `NEEDS_QUOTING` regex in `src/lib/csv.ts` was missing the double quote character. According to RFC-4180, fields containing commas, double quotes, or newlines must be wrapped in quotes. When a title contained a double quote (like `My Issue \"Quote\"`), it wasn't being quoted, causing CSV parsers to break on the unescaped quote and shift columns.\n\n**The fix:** Changed the regex from `/[,\\r\\n]/` to `/[\",\\r\\n]/` to include double quotes in the set of characters that trigger quoting. Now fields with double quotes are properly wrapped in quotes and any embedded quotes are doubled (e.g., `\"` becomes `\"\"`), which is the correct CSV escaping.",
